  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nPenicillins\n\nChief Complaint:\nAbnormal labs\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMs ___ is a ___ h/o tobacco use,\nhypothyroidism, presenting from her PCP with with acute anemia\n(hb 5.4, most recent prior hgb was nl in ___ in the setting of\n6 month history of loss of appetite, nausea, vomiting and 30 lbs\nweight loss over 3 months.  Pt states that she went to her PCP\nfor evaluation of wt loss, and anemia was discovered during w/u\nfor the wt loss.  While at her PCPs office, she states she felt\ndizzy however did not have any other sxs. She has had no \nappetite\nrecently, states everything smells bad.  She also endorses\nnon-bloody emesis, ___ x ___ m.  She denies SOB, CP, abd \npain,\ncough, diarrhea.  No bloody or black stools.  Per notes, she is\nnot up to date on her colonoscopy or pap smear however is\nfollowed at ___ for breast cysts and reportedly has had\nbiopsies in the past which has been negative.  \n\nIn the ED, initial vitals were: 96.8 72 91/31 16 100% RA. \nPressures dropped to systolic 77 however improved to 100 at the\ntime of transfer.  Rectal exam was notably heme neg.  Labs were\nnotable for crit 21.0-->26.3 with 1 u PRBCs, plts 128, AST 52,\nLDH 407, Iron 17, ferritin 18, normal hapto, nl bili.  CT C/A/P\nshowed small to moderate bilat pleural effusions, nodular breast\ntissue, 2 mm pulm nodule.  \n\nOn the floor, pt has no complaints.  She tells me she started\nmirtazipine yesterday.  She expresses concerns regarding dust in\nher apartment causing her asthma to flare on occasion, but \nstates\nthat it is generally well controlled.\n\nReview of systems:\n(+) Per HPI\n(-) Denies fever, chills, night sweats. Denies headache, sinus\ntenderness, rhinorrhea or congestion. Denies cough, shortness of\nbreath. Denies chest pain or tightness, palpitations. Denies\ndiarrhea, constipation or abdominal pain. No recent change in\nbowel or bladder habits. No dysuria. Denies arthralgias or\nmyalgias. 10 pt ros otherwise negative.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nIron Deficiency Anemia\nDuodenitis\nDuodenal ulcers\nWeight loss",
